Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:23:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(app): an MCP move_model tool places and turns an
 imported part (#716)

move_model { name, position, rotation? } runs the GUI's MoveModel command
through the document History, so a headless move is one undo step and every
refusal is the command's own text (a fixture, a work offset, the machine
table, an unknown name, a rotation that is not a quaternion). An omitted
rotation keeps the part's current one. The reply lists the stock that moved
with the part (stock made from it, or a one-part document's stock), read
from the new MoveModel::following_stock().

Pinned by crates/app/tests/mcp_model.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
